Boots of Stealth?  Gum shoes!

I suggest the name Klouseau (or however it's spelled, I know it is supposed
to be a 'C') from the Pink Panther series.  Main weapon?  Clumsiness, of
course.  

    "Does your dog bite?"  (with a bad heavy French accent)
    The big dog hits the Klouseau.
    "I thought you said your dog did not bite!"

The Klouseau might also be in the class of shape-changers, taking on various
disguises.  But, he wouldn't be like the chameleon because he wouldn't have
the special abilities of the mimicked monster.  Furthermore, he would not
change from one monster to another while you are around.

    You hit the nymph.  Hey!  The nymph turns out to be a Klouseau.

By reading the bones files, the Klouseau could be investigating the
disappearances of previous nethack victims.  By reading the date stamp of
the bones files he could ask "the night of the twelfth" questions.
And, what if Klouseaus had a particular knack of stumbling over traps
and secret doors?

    "A booomb!?"  The Klouseau finds a land mine.

If you polymorph yourself into a Klouseau, you probably should have problems
wielding the right weapon, occasionally dropping it.  You might also fall
down (and up) stairs even when you are not overloaded.  I would not suggest
standard intrinsic confusion, though.

    You attempt to wield the +5 short sword, but get the lamp instead.

    As you read the scroll, it disappears.  You get a paper cut.  --more--
    You drop your mace as you scream in pain.

(A "scream in pain" might scare and awaken monsters?)  As an advantage,
though, maybe as a Klouseau you might accidentally remove a cursed piece
of armor.

Dare I suggest 'Kato' sidekicks as well.

    The Kato misses the Klouseau.   "Not now, Kato!"

Maybe as a Klouseau you might have a small possibility of being plagued
by a Kato who hits but usually doesn't do much damage.  Of course, like
other familiars and tamed monsters, you'd be advised not to fight back.

    You become a Klouseau.  The dog misses.  --more--
    Wait!  Why, it's Kato in disguise!

